{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130768-2ed-development-sos-grimoires-discussion","id":1130768,"title":"2ed Development SoS Grimoires Discussion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-18T04:37:12-07:00","id":1130768,"title":"2ed Development SoS Grimoires Discussion","content":"I know that this is a bit late, but I don't like the tone of the other thread. So, here we go!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/grimoires-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/grimoires-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\"> Grimoires! [Mage: The Awakening] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/grimoires-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/grimoires-mage-the-awakening/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I personally am excited to see the new types of grimoires. Astral grimoires and even living ones? Very cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T10:15:46-07:00","id":1135195,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious about the Mood: Close to Home. I'm really looking forward to seeing stuff that leaves a Mage scratching their head even when it emanates from the Supernal. I really like the idea of being able to create in house weirdness without poking through other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T10:26:22-07:00","id":1135494,"title":"","content":"Ah, indeed. For anyone that is more into the lore of the game or likes digging just a touch deeper than the surface, SoS definitely seems like where it's at. As to the grimoire section, I really like that they've expanded our options from 1e. In 1e you get the idea of what a grimoire should seem like in general (not just a generic book with rotes in it). This time, however, you get to mess with some of those options. Palimpsests specifically seem like great opportunities for mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T10:29:02-07:00","id":1135495,"title":"","content":"Right? If you cast a palimpsest with one Potency it's different than if you cast it with two Potency. So, what are all the variables and how high can I get Potency to keep exploring just this one spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T11:09:44-07:00","id":1135511,"title":"","content":"And then it gets even funkier when you start messing with the duration. And don't even get me started on scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T04:47:49-07:00","id":1136888,"title":"","content":"I hope we get some sample Palimpsests, that would really help me get what they are supposed to be and how they are intended to work. At the moment I am not sure how these 'blended effects' manifest, though I am incredibly curious. My first take was that it was like a whole separate spell effect took place. For example I might use my new Grimoire to cast a Space Ward over my house, only to see a Life spell come into being at the same time, encouraging all the plants within the Warded area to grow at super fast rates. On second examination it seems to be more about the original spell being changed to incorporate the 'extra' Arcana rather than a second effect though, so perhaps the Ward keeps out living things rather than Space magic, like a poor mans Ban? <br /> <br /> Also I am unsure if these blended effects are meant to be the same each time the spell is cast, or if the ST is supposed to change it up each time (supposedly with a strong theme so the Caster has at least some idea of what might happen). Both could be fun, though not all players will like that element of randomness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T17:42:28-07:00","id":1137134,"title":"","content":"My expectation is that the effects aren't random once you've figured out the mystery (whether by trial and error or through scrutinizing it, or both). There's not really much of a mystery to strict randomness. I mean, who would go out of their way to create palimpsests if they were only going to create random effects every time you used them?<br /> <br /> I do have to say, I wasn't expecting them to introduce the possibility of artificial intelligence with grimoires. That's pretty interesting. If nothing else, that's probably the closest you can come to a dynamic spell without actually using dynamics. At least, as far as I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T18:58:15-07:00","id":1137154,"title":"","content":"Cognoscente is <i>perfect</i>. It is something I didn't know I wanted, but now I do. It might even convince me to play a non-Mastigos.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I wonder if Hemingway is taken as a Shadow Name?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T19:44:40-07:00","id":1137165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130768-2ed-development-sos-grimoires-discussion#post1130768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astral grimoires and even living ones? Very cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Yes, they are.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> What? I'm not doing anything suspicious. <br /> <br /> ... <br /> <br /> Maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T01:40:14-07:00","id":1137240,"title":"","content":"I'm not entirely convinced &quot;Haunted Grimoire&quot; is really worth it as written. For a weak spirit you're probably getting less free steps in the primary factor than if you just cast the spell, and one strong enough to provide a decent benefit is probably going to win the clash of wills and escape the first time someone uses it.<br /> <br /> Maybe if it just <i>added</i> it's rank to the primary factor on top of what the mage gets...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}